  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN275.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">makaṭpōkkiya cevili colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the foster mother said who had let [her] daughter go.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN275.1">
        <l>ōṅkunilait tāḻi malkac cārttik</l>
        <l>kuṭaiyaṭai nīriṉ maṭaiyiṉa <supplied>ḷe</supplied>ṭutta</l>
        <l>paranta vallaip panteṟin tāṭi</l>
        <l>yiḷamai ta<supplied>kai</supplied>maiyai vaḷamaṉai kiḻatti</l>
        <l>pitirvai <supplied>nī</supplied>rai veṇṇī rukeṉa</l>
        <l>yāntaṟ kaḻaṟuṅ kālait tāṉṟa</l>
        <l>ṉammalai yiṉcoṟ kaḻaṟalai yiṉṟi</l>
        <l>yiṉṉuyir kalappak kūṟi naṉṉutal</l>
        <l>peruñcōṟ ṟillat toruṅkiva ṇirāa</l>
        <l>ḷēti lāḷaṉ <supplied>kā</supplied>ta ṉampit</l>
        <l>tiraḷaṟai yiruppait toḷḷai vāṉpūk</l>
        <l>kuruḷai yeṇki <supplied>ṉī</supplied>riṉaṅ kavarum</l>
        <l>vemmalai yaruñcura <supplied>na</supplied>mmiva ṇoḻiya</l>
        <l>virunila ṉuyirkku miṉṉāk kāṉa</l>
        <l>neruṉaip pōkiya perumaṭat takuvi</l>
        <l>yaitaka lalkuṟ ṟa<supplied>ḻai</supplied>yaṇik kūṭṭuṅ</l>
        <l>kūḻai noccik kīḻa teṉmakaḷ</l>
        <l>cempuṭaic ciṟuviral varitta</l>
        <l>vaṇṭaluṅ kāṇṭirō kaṇṇuṭai yīrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="2a-c">She who [used to] cook with water near the canopy,</l>
        <l corresp="1">joining [more] so that the high level in the jar increased,</l>
        <l corresp="2d-3">playing by throwing the ball into the spreading Allai creepers she had raised,</l>
        <l corresp="6">she who, at the time I remonstrated with her:</l>
        <l corresp="4">“you with the conduct of youth, lady of the prosperous house,</l>
        <l corresp="5">you scatter-brain, sprinkle [some] fresh(?) water,”</l>
        <l corresp="7">without mouthing her sweet words in opposition to us,</l>
        <l corresp="8">talked so that [our] sweet lives mingled,  she with good forehead</l>
        <l corresp="9">is not here together [with us] in the house of great rice,</l>
        <l corresp="10">believing in the love of a stranger,</l>
        <l corresp="15">she prone to great innocence who went [away] yesterday</l>
        <l corresp="14">to the unpleasant forest where the vast ground sighs [with heat],</l>
        <l corresp="13">while we stayed behind , to the difficult desert of hot mountains,</l>
        <l corresp="12">where a large group of bears with young ones seizes</l>
        <l corresp="11">the hollow white flowers of the mahua tree on the round rocks,</l>
        <l corresp="17">my daughter, below(?) the short Nocci tree</l>
        <l corresp="16">from which she joins the foliage to [her] wonderfully broad hips as a decoration,</l>
        <l corresp="19ab">have you seen the Vaṇṭal [lines] too</l>
        <l corresp="18">that [her] little fingers drew into the red side,</l>
        <l corresp="19cd" rend="indent5">you who have eyes?</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
